# Party banter, act 2 (story/banter.gd): one exchange between two or three companions, played now and then on entering an area, once each. Every node opens
# with its act's gate and both speakers, so an exchange that can't be heard comes out empty and is skipped; any file named party_* plays anywhere.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ act2_01_silas_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:delphine_ravelle and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:silas_vane: Three-card monte's all in the wrist, friend. Though your floating chap keeps mouthing where the queen went.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Your Foolishness has no lips. And he only cheats when the billing is dull.
interject name:silas_vane: We both signed the fine print before the Express ever hit the valley, Delphine.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: At least your creditor stays out of sight. Mine critiques my needlework from the cheap seats.
interject name:silas_vane: Keep your stitches tight. When the tab comes due, we'll burn the casino down together.
endif
-> END

~ act2_02_tobin_cordelia
if name:tobin_hayward and name:cordelia_skein and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: Leave off the crimson thread, Cordelia. I'm binding this scrape with bog-moss.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Hold still. I won't let good blood clot under a clump of wet peat.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You treat your friends like prize turnips. Always prodding the rind to see what oozes.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Be reasonable, darling. I offered two vials of reagent for one thimble of your sap.
interject name:tobin_hayward: My sap stays in my seams. Tuck your extra sleeves in before you snag a bramble.
endif
-> END

~ act2_03_delphine_rook
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:rook_coldwake and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:delphine_ravelle: This road's all slick clay, Rook, and my hem is taking on mud.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Culvert's blocked three yards back. Watch the ditch.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: In Picco we laid red velvet when the ground misbehaved. We didn't issue the puddles a summons.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Velvet's poor for drainage. Keep by my shield till the gravel starts.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A gentleman with a door-knocker on his arm. If it clacks by itself again, I'm bowing to the ditch.
endif
-> END

~ act2_04_lucan_tobin
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:tobin_hayward and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Forgive the liberty, Tobin, but your burlap has a distinguished bouquet today. Nine out of ten.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That's dried yarrow, three field mice, and sour turnip from the ditch.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: A subtle vintage. And note that Barnaby never once chews your hem.
interject name:tobin_hayward: He knows if he pulls a thread, I'll weave a little straw hound and flick its ears.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, don't tell him that. He already thinks the thunder is personal.
endif
-> END

~ act2_05_cordelia_rook
if name:cordelia_skein and name:rook_coldwake and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:cordelia_skein: Rook, darling, your chest hasn't risen since the last milestone.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Slipped my mind. Give me a second to draw a proper draught.
interject name:cordelia_skein: If you've no pulse to chart, might I take a scraping of that grave-wax on your knuckles?
interject name:rook_coldwake: That wax is for frostbite and soft joints, Cordelia. Not for your vials.
interject name:cordelia_skein: A pity. If your fingers ever thaw too far, I promise to have the remedy ready.
endif
-> END

~ act2_06_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Your silk notes vanish within the hour, Cordelia. A leather journal keeps a grade for posterity.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Grading a horror seven out of ten for posture is hardly anatomy, darling.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Posture reveals the whole temperament of the quarry. Why are all six of your eyes on Barnaby?
interject name:cordelia_skein: His fur has a delightful sheen, Lucan. And he just yipped at a patch of mushrooms.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: An omen. Or someone dropped a piece of cheese along the track.
endif
-> END

~ act2_07_tobin_silas
if name:tobin_hayward and name:silas_vane and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: Hold still. No, you hold still. That censer's throwing sparks two inches from my collar.
interject name:silas_vane: Easy. I shortened the chain three links and filled a bucket from the ditch, just in case.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Your bitter herbs smell like the gout tonics they sell off painted wagons.
interject name:silas_vane: Best dockside cure in Kalero, Tobin. Clears the lungs, assuming you've got a pair.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Stick to cards, Silas. Leave the curing to folk who know a root from a tinderbox.
endif
-> END

~ act2_08_tobin_cordelia_lucan
if name:tobin_hayward and name:cordelia_skein and name:lucan_houndstooth and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:tobin_hayward: This primrose on my cuff opened another petal since the Crooked House. This soil shouldn't feed a weed.
interject name:cordelia_skein: A thrilling anomaly, Tobin! Let me clip one stamen for testing.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Put the lancet away, if you please, Cordelia. One does not prune a gentleman's sleeve on the march.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Listen to the wolf, girl.
interject name:cordelia_skein: You're both dreadfully protective of a little chlorophyll. It does suit the burlap, though.
endif
-> END

~ act2_09_silas_rook_delphine
if name:silas_vane and name:rook_coldwake and name:delphine_ravelle and flag.vessla_slain and flag.act2_done < 5
interject name:silas_vane: Twelve tallies in my ribs since the Express crashed, Rook, and your ledger's still on page four.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Chalk on bone smudges in the damp, Silas. It wouldn't pass an audit.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: And neither of you leaves room for art, darlings. That's why I take a button off every monster.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Unlogged salvage, that. Though if you're short on thread, there's waxed twine in my shield strap.
interject name:silas_vane: Hear that, Delphine? Stick with the Third Barrow Watch and he'll have us filing receipts by supper.
endif
-> END
